ue aren't good  things we are third in the world for  climate denial behind Saudi Arabia and  Indonesia among a group of 25 countries  that were surveyed it's not an  achievement to be proud of we are one of  the few wealthy Western countries that  allows advertising for medications on  television directly to consumers this is  not a distinct  that we should be proud of and to be  super thorough there are some studies  which show that there is a net benefit  to society and to the economy for  advertising for antidepressants on  television okay so this is complex I'm  against these types of ads as a general  rule but I have read some studies which  say that when you have advertising for  antidepressants on television on the one  hand usually the ones being advertised  are the ones that have not gone generic  and that are the most profitable ones so  yes you have this impact where people  see an ad for a particular  antidepressant and they go to their  doctor and that's the one that they  asked for and we can argue that that's  not necessarily in the patient's best  interest it'd be better if the doctor  without any influence from the patient  evaluated the available medications and  decided which one was best but there are  peer-reviewed studies which say that  when you have direct-to-consumer  television advertising for  antidepressants it actually helps to get  people who are depressed on  antidepressants who otherwise would not  and that there is a measurable societal  benefit to that there's a measurable  economic benefit it reduces absenteeism  at work for example depression is  connected with other medical conditions  which can be expensive to treat it  reduces those by virtue of getting more  people on antidepressants so I think  that if that's the case if we believe  that those studies are accurate you can  achieve a lot of that with more general  sort of nonprofit ads which say if you  have these symptoms there are  medications talk to your doctor your  doctor can recommend something that  could be useful  probably in combination with  psychotherapy for example so you could  probably get a lot of the benefit the  societal benefit the general benefit  that there is for people who are  suffering from depression seeking  treatment for it without allowing  individual for-profit big pharmaceutical  companies to market the most profitable  pills that they have directly to  consumers but anyway good for Trump  right I mean it's a small victory I will  gladly take it and  we'll gladly play it praise Donald Trump  for it in the middle of what is  otherwise a wholly disastrous and  embarrassing presidency period and if  Trump does something again that I agree  with I will be sure to let you know  we've got a great program for you today  I am going to be opening up the phone  lines after the break I know that there  are more people than ever who are trying  to get a hold of me on the program which  is nice it's flattering in many ways  later on in the program we will answer  some audience questions including a very  popular question that comes in from a  lot of people in the audience why does  the David Pakman show have a  disproportionately male audience and  there is actually a lot of interesting  data behind that will also answer some  other questions and then we've got a  great bonus show today as well for our  members and patrons we'll talk about  issues of discrimination within the  Boston police force will not come as a  surprise to many people who know the  city of Boston we will talk about what  is being described as a pokeymon region  in adults who played Pokemon as kids  also on the bonus show we will talk  about the reopening of an investigation  into Donald Trump's handling of  hurricanes in Puerto Rico and the United  States Virgin Islands all of those  stories and more later on on the bonus  show in the immediate I look forward to  hearing from folks on the phones right  after this quick break if you love  learning